{
  "name": "How to make your home safe for a walker",
  "step": [
    {
      "name": "Step 1",
      "text": "Making your home safe for a walker really comes down to creating clear paths and minimizing anything that could cause a trip. Start by looking at the routes someone would take most often. Are there throw rugs that could slide or catch a wheel? Loose rug edges are a big no-no, so secure them or just get rid of them. Clutter is another huge one — clear out those hallways and make sure furniture isn't blocking main walkways. It's also super important to have good lighting, especially in areas like hallways, stairs, and bathrooms. Sometimes, just rearranging furniture can make a world of difference. For bigger changes, like widening doorways or making bathroom modifications, that's when a professional like us at HH Remodeling LLC can step in. We can help assess what’s needed and make those changes so your home truly supports safe movement. Don't wait until a fall happens; a little proactive planning goes a long way. If you’re unsure where to start, give us a call at 303-505-0866 for a home evaluation.",
      "@type": "HowToStep",
      "position": 1
    }
  ],
